Subsea inspection services help operators evaluate the condition and reliability of underwater infrastructure, including pipelines, risers, offshore platform foundations, and subsea equipment. These services identify corrosion, structural damage, burial-depth changes, seabed movement, and other conditions that can affect asset performance.

Demand is supported by the need to reduce unplanned downtime, improve operational safety, and maintain critical offshore infrastructure. Technological advances in remotely operated vehicles (ROVs), autonomous underwater vehicles (AUVs), artificial intelligence, and digital inspection platforms are also changing how inspection data is collected and analyzed. North America held the largest market position in 2025, supported by offshore oil and gas activity and established inspection capabilities.

